{"id":"b538137d-13ed-4fba-b3ce-6de990f8723a","type":"level","createdDate":"2026-07-13T16:20:17.902Z","createdBy":"chaitanya.ponnapati@codeninjas.com","lastModifiedDate":"2026-07-13T16:20:17.902Z","lastModifiedBy":"chaitanya.ponnapati@codeninjas.com","attributes":{"tags":["CREATE"],"title":"Level 1","sequence":1,"activity":{"id":"8f5ec790-fc11-43f2-a6fc-3ed496b49a31","type":"activity","sequence":2,"group":{"id":"8f5ec790-fc11-43f2-a6fc-3ed496b49a31","type":"build","name":null,"sequence":5,"subgroups":[{"id":"8f5ec790-fc11-43f2-a6fc-3ed496b49a31","type":"subgroup","sequence":1,"name":"build 1","steps":[{"id":"5c56d6c8-e9b0-4ca9-8140-1b10f2c4d48b","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">❓ Did you drag the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">[set background color to]</strong><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\"> block </span><em style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">inside</em><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\"> the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">[on start]</strong><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\"> container block?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/bxv1ggb1.55s.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>❓ Did you select a color for your background?</p><p>❓ Did you click ▶<strong><em> </em></strong>to see the background color update?</p>","instructions":"<p>Add a background color to this project! </p><p><br></p><p>Open the<strong> Scene </strong>code block menu, drag a<strong> [set background color to] </strong>block inside the<strong> [on start]</strong> block, then click the gray bubble to select a color from the palette.</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶<strong><em> </em></strong>to see the color appear on the screen.</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"c4d2a455-565c-4044-8bf1-c497c34cfabe","hints":"<p>❓ After clicking the gray box, did you select the Gallery tab from the top menu?</p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/s1umjja4.u1r.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>❓ Did you drag the <strong>[set sprite to]</strong> block <em>inside</em> the <strong>[on start]</strong> container block?</p><p>❓ Did you click the gray box to select a sprite image?</p><p>❓ Did you explore the Gallery and select an image for the sprite?</p>","instructions":"<p>Add a <strong>sprite</strong> to this project! </p><p><br></p><p>Open the<strong> Sprites </strong>code block menu, drag a<strong> [set sprite to] </strong>block inside the<strong> [on start]</strong> container block, then click the gray box and select a <strong>sprite </strong>from the Gallery tab.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶ to see the <strong>sprite</strong> appear on the screen!</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"6773ff14-07a9-46f7-afa7-80cea8560371","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">❓ Did you try both larger and smaller values for the</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> x</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> and for the</span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> y</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> to see how it changes the sprite’s position?&nbsp; </span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/yaoxw3b2.ovb.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>❓ Did you drag the <strong>[set sprite position to]</strong> block <em>inside</em> the <strong>[on start]</strong> container block, <em>underneath</em> the <strong>[set sprite to]</strong> block?</p><p>❓Did you try out different x and y values to move your sprite’s position?</p>","instructions":"<p>Set the <strong>sprite</strong>’s first position! </p><p><br></p><p>Open the <strong>Sprites </strong>code block menu and drag a<strong> [set sprite position to]</strong> block underneath the<strong> [set sprite to] </strong>block inside the<strong> [on start]</strong> container block.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Click in the white bubbles or use the slider to change the <strong>x</strong> and <strong>y</strong> coordinate values to position the <strong>sprite</strong>.</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶ to see the new position of the <strong>sprite</strong>.</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"0fa8442f-81a8-49c4-9951-04a3764dd253","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">❓&nbsp; Did you drag the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">[play sound]</strong><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\"> block </span><em style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">inside </em><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">[on start]</strong><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\"> container block </span><em style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">underneath </em><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">the other blocks?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/rgmzgxzu.zmf.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>❓ Did you select a new sound that you like from the the <strong>[play sound]</strong> block?</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sensei Pro Tip</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">💡 The </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">[play sound]</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> block’s playback mode parameter should be left as </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">[until done]</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> so the code that follows this block does not run until the sound has finished playing. Ninjas will explore other playback mode options in a later level.</span></p>","instructions":"<p>Add a sound to this project! </p><p><br></p><p>Open the<strong> Music </strong>code block menu and drag a<strong> [play sound]</strong> block inside the <strong>[on start]</strong> container, underneath the other blocks.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Click the ⏷ on the<strong> [ba ding] </strong>value to open the drop down menu<strong><em>, </em></strong>then<strong><em> </em></strong>select a sound for this project. Allow the sound to play <strong>[until done]</strong>. This will pause the code from running, until the sound has finished playing.</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶ to hear the <strong>sound</strong> play in this project.</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"d12dad05-13f2-4b2e-9a7a-ffd575d4b148","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">❓&nbsp; Did you drag the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">[start screen effect]</strong><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\"> block </span><em style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">inside </em><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">[on start]</strong><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\"> block </span><em style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">underneath </em><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">the other blocks?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/wbqmimh2.g53.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>❓ Did you select a new screen effect that you like from the the <strong>[start screen effect]</strong> block?</p>","instructions":"<p>Add a screen effect to this project! </p><p><br></p><p>Open the<strong> Scene </strong>code block menu and drag a<strong> [start screen effect]</strong> block inside the <strong>[on start]</strong> container block underneath the other blocks.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Click the ⏷ on the<strong> [confetti] </strong>value to open the drop down menu<strong><em>, </em></strong>then<strong><em> </em></strong>select a screen effect for this project.</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶ to see the <strong>screen effect</strong> in action.</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"d101d079-275e-4c6e-af17-6ac73b569a2e","hints":"<p>❓&nbsp; <span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;Did you select different sounds in the</span><strong style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\"> [play sound] </strong><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">block to see how quickly your sprite image changes?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/0i3zeluq.nz0.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja:</strong></p><p>❓ Did you explore the gallery and select a new image that you like?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sensei Pro Tip</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>💡 The <strong>[set sprite image to]</strong> block does not add a new sprite, it only updates the image of the existing sprite.</p><p>💡 Depending on the sound, the sprite image may update too quickly for the ninja to see. Guide ninjas to try out different sounds to be able to see the switch from the first image to the second image.</p>","instructions":"<p>Switch up how the sprite looks!&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Open the<strong> Sprites </strong>code block menu, drag a<strong> [set sprite image to]</strong> block inside the<strong> [on start]</strong> container block underneath the other blocks, then click the gray box to select a new <strong>sprite </strong>image from the Gallery tab.</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶<strong><em> </em></strong>to see the sprite’s image change after the sound and screen effect.</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"c1843cd7-8551-4eb5-ae09-9eb0b6cb0e54","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">❓ Did you use different </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">x</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> and </span><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">y</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> values so that the sprite moves to a new position?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/quyqj1os.5xd.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja:</strong></p><p>❓ Which value makes the sprite move left and right? Up and down?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sensei Pro Tip</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>💡 Remind ninjas that they can use the slider to select new&nbsp;x and y positions of the sprite.</p>","instructions":"<p>Move the sprite to a different position after its image changes!&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Open the<strong> Sprites</strong> code block menu and drag a<strong> [set sprite position to] </strong>block underneath the <strong>[set sprite image to]</strong> block inside the <strong>[on start] </strong>container<strong> </strong>block.</p><p><br></p><p>Click in the white bubbles or use the slider to change the <strong>x</strong> and <strong>y</strong> coordinate values to position your <strong>sprite</strong>.</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶ to see the <strong>sprite</strong> move from one position to another.</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"4c0800a6-f644-49f3-ab54-cac49967e1fa","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">❓ Did you drag the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">[sprite say]</strong><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\"> block </span><em style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">under </em><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">[set sprite position to]</strong><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\"> block?</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/gk344mmc.jjf.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja:</strong></p><p>❓ What should your sprite say?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sensei Pro Tip:</strong></p><p>💡 Any block that refers to a <strong>sprite </strong>needs to come after its<strong> [set sprite to] </strong>block. </p>","instructions":"<p>Make the <strong>sprite</strong> say something! </p><p><br></p><p>Open the <strong>Sprites </strong>code block menu and drag a<strong> [sprite say] </strong>block underneath the other blocks inside the <strong>[on start]</strong> block. Click in the white bubble and type something for your <strong>sprite</strong> to say.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶ to see what your <strong>sprite</strong> says on screen.</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null},{"id":"36e10800-7dd1-4a1a-852d-9066d4e04b72","hints":"<p><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">❓ Did you drag the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">[splash]</strong><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\"> block to the </span><em style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">top</em><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\"> of the code blocks already inside the </span><strong style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\">[on start]</strong><span style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0);\"> container block?</span></p>","senseiHelp":"<p><strong>Solution</strong></p><p><img src=\"https://assets.codeninjas.com/clm/assets/images/ypfpg1qo.qnh.png\"></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ask the ninja:</strong></p><p>❓ Why is it helpful to include a splash screen at the beginning of your project?</p><p>❓ What information would be helpful for your user to know?</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Sensei Pro Tip</strong>:&nbsp;</p><p>💡 The splash screen should appear at the beginning of the project, and can be cleared by clicking the A button or pressing either the space key or the Z key on the keyboard.</p><p>💡 Guide ninjas to create a splash screen that is related to the sprite they are using.</p>","instructions":"<p>Add a <strong>splash </strong>screen to the beginning of&nbsp;this project! </p><p><br></p><p>Open the<strong> Game </strong>code block menu, drag a<strong> [splash] </strong>block inside the <strong>[on start]</strong> container block at the top of the code.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Click in the white bubble and type the name of this project or a message you want to display at the beginning of this project.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Click ▶<strong><em> </em></strong>to see the <strong>splash </strong>screen in action. Then, press the A button to exit the splash screen and see the rest of this project.</p>","text":null,"type":null,"image":null,"videoUrl":null,"mediaType":null,"questions":null,"badges":null,"reflectionQuestions":null}],"title":"Spooky Effects","project":{"editor":{"filters":[{"name":"sprites","active":false,"blocks":[{"name":"spritescreate"